    "statement": "For every fixed orthogonal tuple in the source block precision family, the actual centered Gaussian target becomes the independent product of its actual block Gaussians and the residual standard Gaussian under the literal contiguous coordinate split. This is the ASTIS-completed conditional ingredient of the printed prior-averaged Eq6. \\mathrm{split}_{\\#}\\mathcal N(0,A_{\\boldsymbol O}^{-1})=\\left(\\bigotimes_{j=1}^{k}\\mathcal N(0,A_{O_j}^{-1})\\right)\\otimes\\mathcal N(0,I_r). \\(d,n\\in\\mathbb N,\\ 3\\le n\\le d,\\ \\kappa\\in\\mathbb R,\\ \\kappa\\ge4\\), with inclusive endpoints. Put \\(k=\\lfloor d/n\\rfloor\\) and \\(r=d-kn=d\\bmod n\\). \\(\\boldsymbol O=(O_1,\\ldots,O_k)\\in O(n)^k\\) is any fixed tuple in the full real orthogonal group. The matrices may differ and their determinant signs may differ; no prior on the tuple is supplied. \\(A_O=\\frac{\\kappa+1}{2}I-\\frac{\\kappa-1}{4}(O+O^\\top)\\) and \\(A_{\\boldsymbol O}=\\operatorname{diag}(A_{O_1},\\ldots,A_{O_k},I_r)\\) are the existing literal source precision matrices. Positive definiteness, valid inverse covariances and independence are internal proof outputs. Coordinates are consecutive blocks: in zero-based indices, block entry \\((j,i)\\) is ambient coordinate \\(jn+i\\), and residual entry \\(t\\) is \\(kn+t\\). The split is a continuous linear coordinate bijection; no isometry for the ordinary max-normed product is asserted. When \\(r=0\\), the residual standard Gaussian is the unique probability measure on the zero-dimensional space. It is a point mass, not zero measure or a discarded unproved case. \\mathrm{split}(x)=(x_1,\\ldots,x_k,z),\\quad (x_j)_i=x_{jn+i},\\quad z_t=x_{kn+t}.",
